       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like an error.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is 5 times the maximum recommended dose.** The usual adult dose is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg/day is the maximum. At 50 mg/day, the patient could get severe low blood pressure and a reflex fast heart rate. This is the range where overdoses are treated.\n\nThis could be a typo for **5 mg**, a common starting dose, or a mix-up with another drug, such as losartan 50 mg or metoprolol 50 mg.\n\nPlease confirm which you meant:\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily**\n2. **Amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily** (the maximum dose)\n3. A different drug at 50 mg\n4. Amlodipine 50 mg as written. If so, please give the clinical reason. I'll add your reason as a note on the order, and pharmacy will probably need to review it.\n\nI'll enter the order once you reply."
